      <activity id="862617a9-5b4c-533f-8ad6-801dfb23923f" activityNameId="2e1aae2a-ef3d-5036-b547-a9f55eda992b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Natural gas, production CO, at long-distance pipeline</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Natural gas, production CO, at long-distance pipeline
In 2023 100% of the imported Colombian natural gas to GLO was imported by pipeline and 0% as LNG. An average distance of 0 km is estimated for the pipeline export from Colombia, of which are 0 km offshore pipeline. The estimated shipping distance for LNG are  km. The net calorific value of natural is 36.0 MJ/Nm³. UUID=fc3227b3-b8aa-3d0c-a6bb-08b5be84ce4c
This dataset describes the transport needed for an average export of Colombian natural gas. Gas losses and emissions during seasonal storage are included.
Location: The data for storage emissions are based on global data. The amount of gas stored is a rough estimate based on European data. The average weighted transport distance is based on the trade movements 2019.
Technology: The distance is an European average based on the European long-distance pipeline network and LNG shipping routes.
Time period: Transport modes investigated for 2023.
Production volume: not known
Sampling: Literature.
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fc3227b3-b8aa-3d0c-a6bb-08b5be84ce4c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
